{"name":"Seduction","hex":"#fbf2bf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seduction","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of seducing.","The felony of, as a man, inducing a previously chaste unmarried female to engage in sexual intercourse on a promise of marriage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seduction"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seduction","blocks":[{"text":"In sexuality, seduction means enticing someone else into sexual intercourse or other sexual activity. Strategies of seduction include conversation and sexual scripts, paralingual features, non-verbal communication, and short-term behavioural strategies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg/330px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seduction"},{"title":"Seduction (tort)","blocks":[{"text":"The tort of seduction was a civil wrong or tort in common law legal systems, and still exists in some jurisdictions."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seduction_(tort)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Delila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg/500px-Delila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Delila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg/500px-Delila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Delilah cutting Samson's hair, c. 1460","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADelila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/The_Dark_Triad_Image.png/330px-The_Dark_Triad_Image.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x",